# A link that a loop follows is restricted to its layout by a shape test that rejects marked objects. After that test, the reads of the iteration do not check whether a slot is filled. The store looks at its own slot.
# Outside the loop, two fields of the middle node are deleted and one is added again. So that node carries a mark, and the slot that the iteration stores into is empty.
# Fault injection, testing=AllowMarkedObjects: the shape test of the link lets marked objects pass. The store finds its slot empty and leaves the iteration, so the answers are right.
# With --aot-harden=proof-checks (testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime) what is remembered about the cell is checked again where it is relied on. If the check fails, the process crashes.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: 2 2 tag,flags,up,seen flags,up,tag,seen tag,flags,up,seen
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(PASSING): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=AllowMarkedObjects
# PASSING: 2 2 tag,flags,up,seen flags,up,tag,seen tag,flags,up,seen
# PASSING-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(HELD): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=AllowMarkedObjects,CheckProofsAtRunTime
# HELD: bun: internal AOT error: redundancy elimination check failed
# HELD-NEXT: a load or check that the compiler removed as redundant gives a different result here
# HELD: crashed with SIGABRT
# RUN(WALK): walk f2:Body mechanisms=all
# WALK: = ShapeTest {{*}}rejectsMarkedObjects
# WALK: : L{{*}} @Cell{{*}}isLoopHead=true
# WALK-NOT: = IsSlotFilled
# WALK: = IsSlotFilled {{*}}key="seen"
# WALK-NOT: = IsSlotFilled
# -- source: main.cjs
